meta {
  name: Letterboxd API
}

headers {
  accept: application/json
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
  username: nemoking
  apiKey: 
  bearerToken: 
}

docs {
  # Letterboxd API
  
  Sync Letterboxd data, filter movies, inspect ratings / favorites / statistics,
  and get personalized recommendations (OpenAI when configured).
  
  ## Setup
  
  1. Start the API (`bun run dev`)
  2. Select the **Local** environment
  3. Set `username` to a Letterboxd username
  4. Run **Users → Sync → Sync User** once before reading derived endpoints
     (or **Users → Get User Profile** for lazy sync)
  
  ## Folder layout
  
  Mirrors API path nesting:
  
  - **Health & public helpers** — `/health`, `/privacy`, GPT Actions schema
  - **Users** — profile at folder root
    - **Sync** / **Movies** / **Ratings** / **Search** / **Statistics** / **Recommendations**
    - **Favorites** — list + **Directors** / **Genres** / **Years** facets
  
  ## Auth (optional)
  
  When the server has `AUTH_ENABLED=true`, set collection var `apiKey` (sent as `X-API-Key`),
  or switch auth mode to Bearer and use `bearerToken`.
  
  ## Favorites
  
  - **List Favorites** — paginated liked movies (same filters as List Movies)
  - **Directors / Genres / Years** — paginated `{ name, count }` facets
  
  List endpoints default `limit` to 20 (max 100).

  ## Recommendations
  
  - **Get Recommendations** — AI path when the server has `OPENAI_API_KEY` + pgvector;
    otherwise rule-based fallback. Optional fields: `slug`, `movieId`, `year`, `poster`.

  ## ChatGPT Custom GPT Actions
  
  Public helpers (no API key required by default):
  
  - **Privacy Notice** — `GET /privacy` (GPT Builder privacy URL)
  - **OpenAPI GPT Actions Schema** — `GET /openapi-gpt-actions.yaml`
  
  Setup guide: docs/chatgpt-actions.md
  
  Interactive docs: `{{baseUrl}}/docs`
}
